CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 16 single-element fold in trailing decltype: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
N5008 [expr.prim.fold] + [dcl.fct]/8: a fold-expression in a
function's trailing-return-type decltype.  Fold reduction previously
ran only in the method-body pass, which does not process a trailing
return type, so the declaration was dropped with "found no match for
symbol 'sum'".  Now reduced in typecheck_type when the pack is bound;
the single-element instantiation keeps the plain parameter name
([temp.variadic]/5).  A pack of size >= 2 needs the replicated
`$k` value parameters (absent while the return type is checked) and
remains a KNOWNBUG (cpp17_fold_in_trailing_decltype_variadic).
